# Workflow Rules (P3) — Development Process

## W-1 — Iteration Planning Gate (SI-1)

Before any version iteration, L0 MUST write a gap analysis in
`.local/research/` before implementation. It MUST list deficiencies, priorities,
and file-scoped fixes; this is the SI-2–SI-10 entry gate.

## W-2 — Harness-Driven Analysis (SI-2)

Iteration analysis MUST use repository evidence and the built-in evaluator:
```
python -m devolaflow.harness evaluate --ledger .local/telemetry/harness.jsonl --repo . --output .local/research/<cycle>_harness_evaluation.json
```
Run it again for end-of-iteration self-evaluation and store raw JSON in
`.local/research/`. Missing/insufficient evidence MUST remain `INSUFFICIENT`
until resolved or escalated. There is no external-tool or manual fallback
that bypasses the built-in evaluator.

## W-3 — Evaluation Before Release (SI-3)

Every pre-release needs a report covering Code quality (0.20), Architecture
(0.20), Tests (0.20), Maintainability (0.15), Compatibility (0.10), and
Performance (0.15); readiness is weighted composite ≥8.5/10.
External claims MUST NOT rely on a single seeded run; use more than one seeded
run and explicit reproducibility metadata: run identifier, caller-supplied salt
when present, source repository, and suitable variance or uncertainty evidence;
metadata or uncertainty evidence is `INSUFFICIENT`, never `PASS`; generated IDs
MUST NOT be called experimental salts.

## W-4 — Harness Regression Guard (SI-4)

Changes to selector/config/schema/SKILL/gate/harness modules MUST run and pass
`make test-harness`; context optimization compares token-injection
distributions, `quantifiable_ratio`, checklist completion, and
reversion/blocker trends with the W-16 baseline. Breaches are release blockers.
The comparison uses the active W-16 harness baseline.
Changes to `src/devolaflow/gate/` also MUST run
`python -m pytest tests/test_gate.py -v`.

## W-5 — Skill Format Coupling (SI-5)

Changes to SKILL.md or CLAUDE.md MUST check its line budget, run `build-skill`
for every HSC-registered adapter, pass `make test-harness`, and pass version
consistency; partial compliance is a violation. Changes to workflow-skill.yaml
also MUST verify core/data-driven adapters from `hosts.yaml` and
`adapter_configs/*.yaml` build within budget.

## W-6 — Context Budget Enforcement (SI-6)

Changes to `context_profiles.yaml` MUST run
`python -m devolaflow.task_adaptive_selector <task_type> --verbose` for every
affected type and verify relevant `critical` sections are retained while
unrelated sections are `skip`.

## W-7 — Iteration Retrospective (SI-8)

After each version release, store a `.local/research/` retrospective covering
gaps, implementation, deferrals/reasons, and learnings.

After W-16 settles cycle evidence, L0 MUST run:

```text
python scripts/archive_research_artifacts.py <cycle-version>
```

and commit the result under `docs/cycle-archive/<cycle-version>/`. Archiving is
idempotent: repeats preserve canonical contents without duplicates or clobbering.

Each cycle archive contains `README.md`, `gap_analysis.md`,
`implementation_plan.md`, `design/`, `harness/`, `evaluation/`, and
`retrospective.md` under `docs/cycle-archive/v<MAJOR>.<MINOR>.0/`.

W-16 settlement MUST precede archive creation. Patch releases create neither
independent baselines nor cycle archives. Historical contents are retained.

Before the retrospective is authored, L0 MUST run the read-only cycle audit
sweep per `references/cycle-audit.md` and record its surfaces and finding count
— including zero — in the retrospective. Findings are parked, not fixed in the
same pass.

## W-8 — Convergence Round Reinforcement (SI-9)

Multi-round convergence MUST use `src/devolaflow/gate/reinforcement.py`, with
at most 5 severity-filtered rules per round. Stagnation for 2+ rounds MUST
escalate to human.

## W-9 — Test-Then-Commit Protocol (SI-10)

Every iteration MUST pass the six SI-10 gates in order:
1. `make test-core` — all tests pass
2. `ruff check src/ tests/`
3. `ruff format --check src/ tests/`
4. `make test-version`
5. `make test-harness`
6. `make check-cursor-skill`

`make precommit-full` aliases `release-preflight`; the Makefile is authoritative
for its six core gates and release-only extras. Single-execution is required:
no test runs twice in one chain, while `make test` remains the full suite.

## W-16 — Harness Baseline Settlement

Each MAJOR or MINOR cycle MUST settle its harness evidence exactly once in
`.local/telemetry/baselines/harness_baseline_<cycle>.json` at close or before
the next PV. Patch releases create no baseline. Every PV compares with that
settled artifact; retain current + previous two Tier-B files and archive older
ones in `docs/cycle-archive/<cycle>/harness/` (A-2.4 Tier C/W-7). Schema bumps
still require a new immutable `layout_invariant_v*.yaml` witness and all
Tier-A witnesses; settlement never regenerates, relocates, or prunes them.

## W-17 — Per-PV Test Cap Discipline (≤+30 NEW test functions per PV; mid-cycle audit at PV-05)

Each PV may add at most **+30 NEW test functions** (parameter expansions do not
count); cycle delta MUST stay ≤**+150**. At midpoint L0 MUST report cumulative
delta and forecast the remainder; if projected over +150, defer non-essential
tests. Count additions with `git diff <previous-tag>..HEAD -- tests/` and
`^\+\s*def test_`.

## W-18 — Ghost-Audit Refresh Precondition

Before CHANGELOG mentions a feature, `tests/ghost/` MUST cover it (S-4
precondition). Add its primary symbol to the current-cycle module, run
`python -m pytest tests/ghost/ -v`, then author the entry;
`tests/ghost/test_rules.py::test_ghost_audit_refresh_present` enforces this.

## W-20 — Env-Flag Reuse vs New-Flag Policy

Before authoring a NEW `DEVOLAFLOW_*` variable, L2 MUST consult
`references/env-flags.md` (canonical inventory) and apply **reuse-first**:

1. Same runtime surface? → REUSE it.
2. R5 pattern applies (read EXACTLY `"1"` + companion probe)? → MUST use
   that parsing and zero-IO off path.
3. Behaviorally orthogonal to every existing flag? → ONLY THEN author new.

A failed orthogonality test is a **W-20 violation**; reviewers MUST reject
(REUSE) or require the argument in the PR body linked to §7.

For a justified flag:

* add it to `references/env-flags.md` §2 in the same PR as its handler;
* add `tests/test_<feature>_disabled_is_noop.py` zero-IO coverage;
* cite it in CHANGELOG `## [vX.Y.Z]` under operator-visible behavior.

## W-21 — Soul-Set Freeze Governance

The Soul layer is frozen at its latest MAJOR/MINOR count. A proposed S-(N+1)
MUST, before landing, be telegraphed in cycle N's retrospective, re-entered
as SI-1 in N+2 with gap/enforcement evidence, and earn SI-3 architecture
≥9.5/10 in N+2. Keep Soul ≤12; later invariants belong in Architecture.
Current freeze: S-1..S-10. W-21 is human-gated; the 60-rule cap is enforced by
`tests/ghost/test_rules.py::test_rule_count_under_cap`.

## W-22 — Grill Mode Activation Contract

Grill mode is a natural-language, one-question interview; its contract and
implementation are `references/grill-mode.md` and
`src/devolaflow/skills/grill_mode.py`. `classify_grill_intent` returns
`GRILL_REQUESTED`, `GRILL_SUGGESTED`, or `NO_GRILL` for explicit, soft, or no
triggers.

### W-22.1 — Parallel-orthogonal composition with plan mode

PLAN and GRILL may coexist; when both are active, L0 MUST grill AC/scope FIRST,
then plan per `references/plan-mode-enforcement.md` §3. W-8/SI-9 and gen-verify
operate on artifacts, not utterances.

### W-22.2 — R5 strict default-OFF for auto-writes

Auto-writes to `CONTEXT.md`, `CONTEXT-MAP.md`, or `docs/adr/` MUST require
session consent; L0 MUST ask before writing. Companion: W-23.

### W-22.3 — 3-condition ADR gate (normative obligation)

For an ADR candidate, L0 MUST call
`devolaflow.skills.grill_mode.qualifies_as_adr(decision)` →
`(qualifies, missing_conditions)`. If false, L0 SHALL skip the offer and
surface failed conditions: Hard to reverse, Surprising without context, and
Real trade-off; all three are required.

### W-22.4 — W-20 env-flag reuse-first preservation

NO new `DEVOLAFLOW_*` flag is introduced: activation is solely
`classify_grill_intent`; see `references/env-flags.md` §2.

## W-23 — Domain Glossary Maintenance

When grill mode resolves a term, L0 MAY update the glossary per
`references/domain-awareness.md` (format/mechanics).

### W-23.1 — Lazy file creation

Create `CONTEXT.md` only for the first term, `CONTEXT-MAP.md` only for 2+
contexts, and `docs/adr/` only after W-22.3 passes. Repo-init MUST NOT create
them; operator consent remains required.

### W-23.2 — Opinionated-term discipline

The glossary MUST select ONE canonical term and list alternatives as `_Avoid_:`
aliases. `detect_fuzzy_terms(plan_text, glossary)` surfaces aliases;
`propose_canonical_term(candidate, glossary)` suggests the canonical term.

### W-23.3 — Project-specific scope

`CONTEXT.md` MUST contain only THIS project's domain terms; general programming
concepts DO NOT belong.

### W-23.4 — CONTEXT.md vs spec.md separation (per A-4)

`CONTEXT.md` is VOCABULARY; `.local/memory/specs/<domain>/spec.md` is BEHAVIOR.
They DO NOT overlap: terms go to `CONTEXT.md`, behavior decisions to
`.local/.agent/active/<id>/spec.md`.

### W-23.5 — Single vs multi-context layout inference

`infer_context_layout(repo_root)` returns `MULTI_CONTEXT` when
`CONTEXT-MAP.md` exists (map wins), `SINGLE_CONTEXT` for `CONTEXT.md`, else
`NO_CONTEXT_YET`; it is the only filesystem probe and MUST raise
`FileNotFoundError` for a missing root (S-5).

## W-24 — Subagent Pattern Selection

At wave decomposition, consult `references/subagent-patterns.md` and
`src/devolaflow/skills/subagent_pattern.py`. Supported patterns: **INLINE**
(one L2 via `Task`) and **FAN_OUT** (one L1, ≤5 parallel L2 tasks). **Teams
are permanently unsupported**: Soul P5 forbids shared state; reversal requires
SI-1, ADR, W-21 cadence, and SI-3 §3.2 ≥9.5/10.

### W-24.1 — Selection contract

`select_pattern(complexity, model_tier, task_count, parallel_independence)`
returns `"INLINE" | "FAN_OUT"` and NEVER `"TEAMS_FORBIDDEN"`; that literal is
reserved for `forbidden_pattern_rationale("TEAMS_FORBIDDEN")`.
### W-24.3 — Pattern 4 permanent-NOT-SUPPORTED rationale

The helper NEVER auto-returns `TEAMS_FORBIDDEN`; callers invoke the rationale
function explicitly for the P5 citation.

Source: v15-ADR-008 §W-24; taxonomy in `references/subagent-patterns.md`.

## W-25 — Host Support Contract Evidence and Revision

`workflow-system/agent/hosts.yaml` owns host identity, tiers, delivery floor,
and extras. A `boundary_bridge` MUST list `captured` or `vendor-doc`
provenance; the latter requires a `provenance_ref` URL, and
`synthetic`/`TBD-audit` cannot substantiate implementation. Adding a host,
channel, or axis MUST update schema, loader/parity tests, and current-cycle
ghost audit before claims. Unsupported capabilities remain `undeclared`,
`designed`, or `broken`; derived manifest views need parity checks. New axes
need design and evidence-backed tests; W-20 governs flags.

Source: v17.4.0 HSC design.

## W-26 — Local-Archive Deletion Safety (C-G4.3)

Deletion is permanently operator-only: no automatic deletion API/workflow for
`tasks`, `feedbacks`, or `research`; planning/clean checks never authorize it.
Runtime MUST NOT invoke `git clean -fdx` or equivalent. Dirty, ambiguous,
missing, unreadable, nested-repository, symlink, protected, or conflicted paths
MUST yield explicit refusal findings and remain in place. `.local/human/` and
`.local/.agent/` are never adapter inputs. See
`references/local-archive.md` §§6–7, `src/devolaflow/local/archive.py`,
`tests/test_local_archive.py`, `tests/test_local_archive_surfaces.py`, and the
current ghost audit.

## W-27 — Local-Archive Mapping Append-Only Behavior (C-G4.4)

Every physical move MUST append a record to its surface ledger:
`.local/tasks/archive-mappings.yaml`, `.local/feedbacks/archive/archive-mappings.yaml`,
or `.local/research/archive/archive-mappings.yaml`. Rows contain increasing
`sequence`, `source`, `destination`, `reason`, `timestamp`; existing rows are
immutable and duplicate source/destination MUST be refused. These are not
`.local/.agent/` handoffs; S-9 remains separate. See
`references/local-archive.md` §8, `src/devolaflow/local/archive.py::append_mapping_record`,
and cited local-archive tests/ghost audit.

## W-28 — Local-Archive Index-Generation Honesty (C-G4.5)

Each surface owns a generated index beside its ledger:
`.local/tasks/INDEX.md`, `.local/feedbacks/archive/INDEX.md`, or
`.local/research/archive/INDEX.md`. Output MUST carry its surface marker
(tasks: `<!-- devolaflow: generated task archive index -->`); only approved
apply may create a missing index. Human-maintained, symlinked, unreadable,
stale, or non-generated indexes MUST produce refusal/drift, never overwrite.
See `references/local-archive.md` §8, `src/devolaflow/local/archive.py::render_index`,
and cited tests/ghost audit.

## W-29 — Retro-Digest Evidence and Consent

Retro-Digest is natural-language only and MUST NOT add a `DEVOLAFLOW_*` flag or
CLI. Extraction MUST preserve verbatim source and repository-relative
provenance; L0 MAY select/label but MUST NOT rewrite it. Default is report-only;
writing `operational.jsonl` requires consent. Benefits stay report-only.
Missing evidence is `INSUFFICIENT`, never `PASS`. See
`references/retro-digest.md`.

## W-30 — Continuous Progress Contract

### W-30(a) — Bounded Wait and Ready-Work Progress

While a long-running external task is active (including CI, installation,
long tests, deployment, or an equivalent operation), agents MUST NOT idle or
meaninglessly poll. Every wait MUST have a timeout, heartbeat, and terminal
abandon/escalation path. When dependencies are satisfied and resources permit,
dispatchers MUST advance ready work instead of waiting.

### W-30(b) — Selective Blocker Isolation

After preflight, an ordinary blocker or `HUMAN_INTERVENE` finding pauses only
its affected item/task. Independent, unaffected siblings MUST continue. Reports MUST
distinguish `dependency-blocked` (waiting for a prerequisite),
`finding-blocked` (an unresolved finding), and `wave conflict` (ownership or
interface overlap). The workflow may stop only when no task can advance, or a
HARD breakpoint, preflight STOP card, `FULL_ROLLBACK`, ownership violation, or
destructive-policy violation requires it. A signed preflight does not waive
hard stops.

Primary references: `workflow-system/agent/references/execution-protocol.md`
§3, `references/decomposition-gate.md` §10, and
`references/wave-dispatch.md` §"Continuous progress and blocker isolation".
